==English==

===Etymology===
By false alteration of either [[tafferel]] or [[aft]] + [[rail]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|nautical}} The curved wooden top of the [[stern]] of a [[sailing]] [[man-of-war]] or [[East Indiaman]], usually [[carved]] or [[decorated]].
# {{context|nautical}} The [[rail]] around the [[stern]] of a [[ship]].
# {{context|nautical}} The [[deck]] area at the stern of a [[vessel]].

====Derived terms====
* [[taffrail log]]

